<div id="ClsCoppercutopenWhatIFound-{{ section.id }}" class="cls-coppercutopen-what-i-found">
  <div class="cls-coppercutopen-what-i-found__trigger-marker" data-cls-coppercutopen-sticky-trigger aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="cls-coppercutopen-what-i-found__inner">
    <div class="cls-coppercutopen-what-i-found__text">
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="cls-coppercutopen-what-i-found__heading">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
        <div class="cls-coppercutopen-what-i-found__body cls-coppercutopen-rte">{{ section.settings.body }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="cls-coppercutopen-what-i-found__media">
      <div class="cls-coppercutopen-what-i-found__photo">
        {%- if section.settings.photo != blank -%}
          <img
            src="{{ section.settings.photo | image_url: width: 1280 }}"
            srcset="
              {{ section.settings.photo | image_url: width: 450 }} 450w,
              {{ section.settings.photo | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w,
              {{ section.settings.photo | image_url: width: 1280 }} 1280w
            "
            sizes="100vw"
            alt="{{ section.settings.photo.alt | escape }}"
            loading="lazy"
            width="{{ section.settings.photo.width }}"
            height="{{ section.settings.photo.height }}"
          >
        {%- elsif section.settings.photo_fallback != blank -%}
          <img
            src="{{ section.settings.photo_fallback | replace: '.jpg', '-900.jpg' | asset_url }}"
            srcset="
              {{ section.settings.photo_fallback | replace: '.jpg', '-450.jpg' | asset_url }} 450w,
              {{ section.settings.photo_fallback | replace: '.jpg', '-900.jpg' | asset_url }} 900w,
              {{ section.settings.photo_fallback | asset_url }} 1280w
            "
            sizes="100vw"
            alt="Macro shot of a cut bottle wall"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if section.settings.caption != blank -%}
        <div class="cls-coppercutopen-what-i-found__caption-wrap">
          <p class="cls-coppercutopen-what-i-found__caption">{{ section.settings.caption | escape }}</p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "What I found",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Nine bottles, nine sellers, one bandsaw"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body",
      "label": "Body copy",
      "default": "<p>I bought nine bottles from nine different sellers. Prices ran from <strong>$19 to $39.</strong> Every listing used the word copper in the title. Four claimed <strong>100% pure copper.</strong> Two claimed lab testing. Five said hand-hammered or handmade.</p><p>Four of the nine responded to a magnet. On two of those, only the cap did — <strong>the body was copper</strong> and the cap was <strong>plated steel</strong>, which is the cheapest possible place to save money and the last place anyone looks.</p><p><strong>Six of the nine</strong> had a coating on the inside wall. You can see it once the bottle is open: a glossy film that stops neatly at the neck, where the spray gun stopped.</p><p>That sixth finding is the one that matters most, and it is the one I did not expect. A lacquered bottle is not a safety story. It is a pointlessness story. The entire <strong>reason</strong> to drink from copper is that the water touches copper. Put a film between the two and you have bought a heavy, expensive, copper-coloured container with a plastic interior — which is the thing most of these <strong>buyers were trying to get away from.</strong></p><p>Seven of the nine contained a metal that was <strong>not copper</strong> somewhere in the bottle: plated steel, a copper skin over aluminium, or copper alloyed down with zinc.</p><p>Two were solid copper the whole way through. Both were machine-pressed. Both were sold as <strong>hand-hammered.</strong></p><p>So the final count is not seven out of nine, or six out of nine. It is nine out of nine. Not one of the bottles I bought was what its listing said it was.</p><p>None of the nine sellers published a lab report. I asked all nine. Two replied. Neither sent anything.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "photo",
      "label": "Photo"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "photo_fallback",
      "label": "Photo fallback filename",
      "info": "Used only if no photo is set above. Must be an asset filename already uploaded to this theme.",
      "default": "copper-bottles-cut-open-macro-wall.jpg"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "caption",
      "label": "Photo caption",
      "default": "Bottle 4 · $27 · listed as 100% pure copper, lab-tested"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "What I found"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
